; `@DEBUG` opens Emuera's three-tab debug dialog, but only in a run started
; with -Debug — otherwise doSystemCommand refuses it
; (GameView/EmueraConsole.cs:1367-1375, and again silently at :1816-1817).
; The sibling `.debug` marker starts this fixture that way.
;
; erars has no dialog, so the two tabs whose content the engine owns are
; printed instead: the stack-trace tab, label for label from GetDebugTraceLog
; (:1788-1812), and the console tab, which is the DEBUGPRINT buffer (:1783).
; The variable-watch tab needs the dialog's interactive grid and is not
; reproduced. §5.16 of docs/research/2026-09-03-emuera-command-gap.md records
; that, and records that each frame reports its own current position — the
; call site, for an outer frame — where Emuera logs the declaration line of
; the function being entered.
@SYSTEM_TITLE
DEBUGPRINTL buffered
CALL SHOWDEBUG
PRINTFORML [%RESULTS%]

@SHOWDEBUG
INPUTS
